"# Jordimp & Co. — full reference

Jordi Marçal Poy — Senior Backend Engineer (Java · Python · AI/LLM).
One-person engineering firm, est. 2017, Barcelona. Languages: English, Español, Català.
Contact: hello@jordimp.net · [GitHub](https://github.com/jordimarsal) · [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/jordi-marsal-poy)

## The building

## F3 — Research & Retrieval

The top floor ships AI like infrastructure: deterministic cores, golden Q/A sets, evals gated in CI. If a model can’t be measured, it doesn’t ship.

Projects:
  - CodebaseRAG (2026): Hexagonal RAG over your own codebase, with a deterministic, eval-first core: ingest, query, and CI-gated retrieval evals. Stack: Python 3.13, FastAPI, pgvector, Qdrant, Ollama, Langfuse, mypy strict. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/codebaserag)
  - Interview Simulator (2026): Voice interview simulator: a local LLM plays the interviewer and Whisper handles transcription, so you can rehearse technical interviews fully offline. Stack: Whisper, Local LLM. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/interview-simulator)

## F2 — Transport & Telemetry

Event pipelines, rate limits and health tracking with honest failure modes. When a dependency goes down, callers know exactly where they stand. Personal study of the Open Gateway telemetry problem. Not Telefónica code. Not production traffic.

Projects:
  - Kafka Adapter Telemetry (2026): Event-driven adapter telemetry: a Kafka gateway + hub pipeline with idempotent Oracle persistence, per-adapter health tracking, alerting, and a live SSE mission-control dashboard. Stack: Java 25, Spring Boot 4.1, Kafka, Oracle, Flyway, Testcontainers, SSE. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/kafka-adapter-telemetry)
  - Redis Toolkit (2026): Rate-limiting toolkit for LLM gateways: atomic token-bucket quotas, pluggable stores, honest failure modes — with a Javalin gateway demo exposing an OpenAI-style endpoint. Stack: Java, Javalin, Redis, Testcontainers. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/redis-toolkit)

## F1 — Tooling & Platform

The workshop floor: a multi-agent SDD harness, CLIs that do one thing well, and tooling kept intentionally small. Everything it needs, nothing it doesn’t.

Projects:
  - Harness Standard (2026): A standardized multi-agent harness for Claude Code and OpenCode: Spec-Driven Development roles (Leader, Spec Author, Implementer, Reviewer) installed into any project with a single command. Stack: Agents, SDD, CLI, Conventions. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/harness-standard)
  - MD Mermaid PDF (2025 - 2026): CLI that renders Markdown with Mermaid diagrams straight to PDF, engineered with TDD, mypy strict and CI. Stack: Python, Markdown, Mermaid, GitHub Actions. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/md-mermaid-pdf)
  - MCP Transparent PNG (2026): MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that makes PNG colors transparent (alpha channel) with rgb/auto/greenscreen modes. Stack: Python 3.13, MCP, Pillow, GitHub Actions. [repo](https://github.com/jordimarsal/mcp-transparent-png)

## Q — Inspections

The inspection floor keeps the quality wall: Lighthouse gauges, test counters, bundle weight and dependency census — audited on a schedule, dated, and hung at the entrance as the ITE plaque. Static-first: the certificate shows the last audit, never a broken promise.


## M — People & Principles

The mezzanine keeps the house rules: SOLID, Clean Code and TDD as daily practice, I/O at the edges, and knowledge that flows across the team.


## F0 — Operations

The ground floor keeps the record: every engagement since 2017, what shipped, and what it was built with. One ledger, four chapters, zero rewrites.


## B — Front Desk

The desk takes three things: senior or staff backend roles, short spec-first engagements, and questions about a floor or a repo. Bring the problem in your own words — if it can’t be written down, it doesn’t start.


